n![](images/f3/f34061f5ffb1c2aaab8728cb51f3dc88df57e1c483e2fae478eb659c220284d2.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{7}{4}$." 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186761453 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761460 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761460 1077 "field-1" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761460 1078 #edb/ref 17592186761453 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761460 1079 #uuid "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761461 1080 "\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761461 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761461 1083 #uuid "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761462 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761456 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761462 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761462 1071 "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in h