\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{3}{2}\\,(1, -1)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -\\frac{3}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(2, -4).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/54/5447bc67b11cfc569d5a04eb6e94164ada1fa82782ba423722a3c6bd01d70e4b.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{2}{2}=1 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=1$." 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761470 1080 "2" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761470 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761470 1083 #uuid "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761471 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761471 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761471 1083 #uuid "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761472 1080 "1" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761472 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761472 1083 #uuid "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761473 1080 "1" 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761473 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547590 17592186576411 true] [17592186761473 1083 #uuid "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848" 13194139547590 175